WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.172 --> 00:00:14.134
Julie and Doug arrived at Tim's house very excited.

2
00:00:18.296 --> 00:00:20.777
The three friends were going to hear Lisa Byrd sing.

3
00:00:25.319 --> 00:00:27.040
Lisa was a famous performer.

4
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.661
"I can't believe Lisa grew up in our town!"

5
00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:34.702
said Julie.

6
00:00:34.722 --> 00:00:41.825
"Her parents own the Byrd Music School where she is performing," said Tim.

7
00:00:41.845 --> 00:00:45.547
"I can't believe our parents are letting us go alone!"

8
00:00:46.288 --> 00:00:46.888
said Doug.

9
00:00:46.908 --> 00:00:53.852
"It's not very far," said Tim, rolling his wheelchair to his desk.

10
00:00:53.872 --> 00:00:58.254
"I take piano lessons there every week."

11
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:01.096
Tim opened a map on his desk.

12
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.842
He followed the streets on the map with his finger.

13
00:01:09.565 --> 00:01:14.589
go north on Oak Street, turn east on Elm Drive, then north on Maple Street."

14
00:01:18.192 --> 00:01:19.113
"Here's a shortcut!"

15
00:01:19.453 --> 00:01:20.053
said Doug.

16
00:01:23.156 --> 00:01:24.797
He pointed to a path through the park.

17
00:01:30.682 --> 00:01:32.764
not a shorter route," said Tim.

18
00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:35.509
"The streets are straight.

19
00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:37.631
The path in the park is squiggly."

20
00:01:37.651 --> 00:01:44.015
"A straight line is the shortest distance between two points," said Julie.

21
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:47.538
Doug looked at both routes on the map.

22
00:01:51.861 --> 00:01:55.544
"I still think it's shorter to go across the park."

23
00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:00.628
"Hmm," said Julie.

24
00:02:03.512 --> 00:02:06.533
"The shortest distance across an area is a diagonal."

25
00:02:08.714 --> 00:02:09.535
She looked unsure.

26
00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:15.237
measure the length of each route on the map."

27
00:02:17.978 --> 00:02:19.059
Tim picked up a ruler.

28
00:02:19.079 --> 00:02:21.920
"I'll measure the streets," he said.

29
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.601
Julie wrote down the lengths of the streets.

30
00:02:27.102 --> 00:02:28.322
Then she added them together.

31
00:02:28.342 --> 00:02:31.764
"The street route is ten centimeters."

32
00:02:34.892 --> 00:02:39.473
"The map scale shows that each centimeter equals two hundred meters," said Tim.

33
00:02:44.435 --> 00:02:46.375
it's two kilometers along the streets."

34
00:02:48.376 --> 00:02:50.156
Doug tried to measure the park path.

35
00:02:56.198 --> 00:02:58.719
hard to follow the squiggly line with the ruler."

36
00:03:00.619 --> 00:03:01.559
Tim shook his head.

37
00:03:01.579 --> 00:03:03.680
"That won't work."

38
00:03:07.222 --> 00:03:08.123
"I have an idea!"

39
00:03:08.303 --> 00:03:08.944
said Julie.

40
00:03:10.525 --> 00:03:12.467
She laid a piece of string over the path.

41
00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.153
Then she marked the path's beginning and end on the string.

42
00:03:19.173 --> 00:03:22.235
"Now we can just measure the string!"

43
00:03:24.417 --> 00:03:26.099
Julie stretched the string straight.

44
00:03:28.301 --> 00:03:31.684
Then Doug used the ruler to measure the distance between the two marks.

45
00:03:33.864 --> 00:03:34.944
"It's two kilometers.

46
00:03:35.124 --> 00:03:37.165
The same distance as the street route!"

47
00:03:38.606 --> 00:03:40.126
The three kids looked at each other.

48
00:03:43.967 --> 00:03:44.707
way should we go?"

49
00:03:45.208 --> 00:03:45.768
asked Tim.

50
00:03:45.788 --> 00:03:49.429
"Through the park!"

51
00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:50.369
said Julie.

52
00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:52.570
She grinned.

53
00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:56.391
"We can hear the birds sing before we hear Lisa
